2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] Usage inside your C++ server
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Add the two files to your build (only standard POSIX sockets).
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Once at start-up:
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] if (!FountainBridge::init()) {
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905]     std::cerr << "Fountain not reachable on :8081\n";
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905]     // keep going without it, or abort
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Anywhere you want to send something to Fountain:
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] std::string msg = R"({"messages":[{"message":"ping","from":"cpp"}]})";
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] FountainBridge::push(msg);
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Anywhere you want to read what Fountain broadcast (non-blocking):
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] std::string line;
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] while (FountainBridge::pop(line)) {
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905]     handleFountainJson(line);   // your parser
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. At exit:
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] FountainBridge::shutdown();
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] No dependencies, no extra threads visible to the rest of your code, and Fountain’s original
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] TCP/NDJSON protocol stays untouched.
2025-11-05 14:25:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
