2025-11-18 16:17:36 [simon@midnightblue] utsname is ok for linux and mac?
2025-11-18 16:17:40 [gpt-5.1-2025] Yes. `uname`/`struct utsname` is standardized by POSIX and works on both Linux and macOS (and other
2025-11-18 16:17:40 [gpt-5.1-2025] Unix-like systems).
2025-11-18 16:17:40 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:17:40 [gpt-5.1-2025] - On macOS, `sysname` is typically `Darwin`.
2025-11-18 16:17:40 [gpt-5.1-2025] - On Linux, `sysname` is typically `Linux`.
