2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] Public C++ embedder-facing changes between V8 13.5 and 14.0 are incremental rather than “huge
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] rewrite,” but there are some things to watch for if you’re targeting both:
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 1. API deprecations / removals
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Some methods are marked `V8_DEPRECATED` in 13.x and may be removed or changed in 14.x.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Typical examples (not exact to those versions, but style-wise):
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	- Old `Isolate::GetCurrent()` / `Context::GetCurrent()` patterns in favor of passing
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] isolates/contexts explicitly.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	- Helpers that used `Local<String>`/`Local<Name>` in looser ways replaced by stricter overloads.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - If you compile your 13.5 embedder with deprecation warnings on, most things that matter for 14.0
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] will already be noisy.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 2. Handle / lifetime patterns
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Continued push toward more explicit handle scope management, fewer “magic” convenience helpers.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Some APIs move to require `Local<Context>` parameters that used to rely on
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] `Context::GetCurrent()` or ambient state.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - More functions demand `Isolate*` arguments even where they were implicit before.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 3. Sandbox / pointer safety
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Ongoing hardening of the sandbox / pointer compression setup.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - If you rely on casting between `void*` / internal fields and C++ pointers, the newer V8 may be
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] stricter or have different expectations about alignment / tagging.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Safer pattern: store only POD or 64-bit integers in internal fields, or use `v8::External`
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] instead of raw pointer games.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 4. Embedder data / external memory
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Tweaks over time in how external memory accounting and GC heuristics work.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - If you call `isolate->AdjustAmountOfExternalAllocatedMemory(...)`, expect slightly different GC
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] behavior, but not interface changes.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Embedder data slots (`SetEmbedderData` / `GetEmbedderData`) are stable, but more code uses them
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] rather than “hidden fields” for engine-internal bookkeeping.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 5. Callbacks and error handling
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Tightening around `v8::FunctionCallbackInfo` usage; some older helper callbacks or ways of
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] throwing exceptions may be marked deprecated.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Strong preference for explicit `TryCatch`, and some helpers returning `MaybeLocal` instead of
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] `Local` (forcing you to check for failure).
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 6. Build / configuration side
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - GN args and public headers may have moved slightly; some defines you relied on in 13.5 might be
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] renamed or removed.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - If you’re statically linking or using snapshots, snapshot-generation tools and flags can change
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] between minor releases.
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] If your `v8io` project already:
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Uses explicit `Isolate*`/`Local<Context>` rather than “current” globals,
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Avoids relying on deprecated APIs,
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Uses `MaybeLocal` responsibly and checks results,
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Stores data via `External` or embedder data rather than raw pointer casts in internal fields,
2025-11-18 16:20:52 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
