2025-11-18 18:53:52 [simon@midnightblue] GetTracingController
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] On recent V8 (including 13.5.x), `v8::Platform::GetTracingController()` is still a pure virtual, so
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] your `NitroPlatformWithPool` must return a valid object, not `nullptr`, or you risk crashes/asserts
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] when V8 touches tracing.
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] You have:
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] v8::TracingController* GetTracingController() override { return nullptr; }
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] Safer options:
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 1. Use V8’s default tracing controller (if available in your build)
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] If your headers expose it:
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] #include <libplatform/libplatform.h>
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] class NitroPlatformWithPool : public v8::Platform {
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] public:
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	NitroPlatformWithPool(size_t threads = std::thread::hardware_concurrency())
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		: pool_(std::make_unique<NitroThreadPool>(threads)),
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		  thread_count_(threads),
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		  tracing_controller_(std::make_unique<v8::platform::TracingController>()) {}
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::TracingController* GetTracingController() override {
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		return tracing_controller_.get();
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	}
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] private:
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::unique_ptr<NitroThreadPool> pool_;
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	size_t thread_count_;
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::unique_ptr<v8::platform::TracingController> tracing_controller_;
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] };
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 2. If you truly don’t care about tracing
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] You still need a live object, but it can be a trivial implementation. The easiest is usually to
2025-11-18 18:54:02 [gpt-5.1-2025] reuse V8’s `platform::TracingController` as above and just ignore its configuration.
