2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] `GetPageAllocator()` must return a single, long‑lived allocator, not a new one each call.
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] Right now you have:
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] v8::PageAllocator* GetPageAllocator() override {
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::cout << "GetPageAllocator" << std::endl << std::flush;
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	return new NitroPageAllocator();
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] }
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] That leaks allocators and doesn’t match V8’s expectations. The platform is supposed to own the
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] allocator object and return the same pointer every time.
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] Make it a member of `NitroPlatformWithPool` and return that:
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] class NitroPlatformWithPool : public v8::Platform {
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] public:
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	NitroPlatformWithPool(size_t threads = std::thread::hardware_concurrency())
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		: pool_(std::make_unique<NitroThreadPool>(threads)),
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		tracing_(std::make_unique<NitroTrace>()),
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		page_allocator_(std::make_unique<NitroPageAllocator>())
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	{
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		std::cout << "NitroPlatformWithPool" << std::endl << std::flush;
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	}
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::PageAllocator* GetPageAllocator() override {
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		std::cout << "GetPageAllocator" << std::endl << std::flush;
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		return page_allocator_.get();
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	}
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] private:
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::unique_ptr<NitroThreadPool> pool_;
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::unique_ptr<NitroTrace> tracing_;
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::unique_ptr<NitroPageAllocator> page_allocator_;
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] };
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:02:55 [gpt-5.1-2025] This way the allocator lives as long as the platform and is reused.
