2025-11-19 10:07:30 [simon@midnightblue] is there a default with monolithic with no platform
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] Yes. You don’t have to provide your own `v8::Platform` at all; you can use V8’s built‑in default
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] platform even when linking against the monolithic library.
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] On non‑embedded builds that’s usually done via the `libplatform` helper:
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 1. Link against `libv8_libplatform` (or the equivalent in your build).
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 2. At startup:
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] #include <libplatform/libplatform.h>
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] int main() {
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::V8::InitializeICUDefaultLocation(nullptr);
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::V8::InitializeExternalStartupData(nullptr);
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	std::unique_ptr<v8::Platform> platform =
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 		v8::platform::NewDefaultPlatform();
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::V8::InitializePlatform(platform.get());
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::V8::Initialize();
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	// create isolate, context, run JS…
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::V8::Dispose();
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 	v8::V8::ShutdownPlatform();
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] }
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] That `NewDefaultPlatform()` gives you a threaded platform with a default page allocator, worker
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] threads, tracing, etc. You don’t need `NitroPlatformWithPool` or `NitroPageAllocator` unless you
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] really want custom behavior.
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] If your monolithic build already includes `libplatform` internally (some configs do), the same API
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] is still used; you just don’t link an extra library.
2025-11-19 10:07:38 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:07:55 [simon@midnightblue] no this is embedded
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] For an embedded build, there isn’t a “magic” default platform you can skip to; you still need to
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] provide a `v8::Platform`. However, you don’t have to implement everything yourself from scratch.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] You effectively have three options:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 1. Use V8’s `libplatform` even in embedded mode
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    If your build still has `libplatform` available, you can use
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] `v8::platform::NewDefaultPlatform()` exactly as in non‑embedded builds. You’re still “embedded”,
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] but you’re using the supplied platform implementation instead of writing one. This is the simplest
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] if your toolchain/storage budget allows linking in that code.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 2. Minimal custom platform that delegates to V8’s default page allocator
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    If you want a small, custom platform but don’t specifically need your own `PageAllocator`, you
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] can:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - Implement `v8::Platform` with:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]      - A foreground `TaskRunner` that just runs tasks on the main thread (or posts to your
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] RTOS/event loop).
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]      - Background `PostTaskOnWorkerThreadImpl` that either:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]        - Runs tasks inline (single‑threaded), or
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]        - Uses your `NitroThreadPool`.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - Return `nullptr` from `GetPageAllocator()` so V8 uses its internal allocator.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - Implement the required timing, tracing, etc. minimally.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    That keeps sandbox / pointer‑compression details in V8 and avoids implementing
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] `GetRandomMmapAddr` and friends.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 3. Fully custom platform + page allocator (what you’re doing now)
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    This is required only if:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - You need custom memory placement (e.g. special RAM regions, MPU configuration), or
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - You have to integrate tightly with an RTOS/allocator.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    Then you must implement:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - `GetPageAllocator()` returning your `NitroPageAllocator`.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025]    - `AllocatePages`, `FreePages`, `SetPermissions`, and a sane `GetRandomMmapAddr` compatible with
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] your `V8ENABLESANDBOX` / `V8COMPRESSPOINTERS` config.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] So to your question “is there a default with monolithic with no platform” in embedded mode:
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] - There is no implicit default: `V8::InitializePlatform` still needs a `v8::Platform*`.
2025-11-19 10:08:18 [gpt-5.1-2025] - The closest to a “default” is either:
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025]   - `v8::platform::NewDefaultPlatform()` (if you can use `libplatform`), or
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025]   - A trivial custom `Platform` that hands `nullptr` from `GetPageAllocator()` and doesn’t override
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025] the memory allocator at all.
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025] If you want, I can outline a minimal embedded `Platform` that doesn’t supply a custom
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025] `PageAllocator` and keeps your thread pool, so you can test the rest of your integration without
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025] fighting sandbox memory layout yet.
2025-11-19 10:08:19 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:09:52 [simon@midnightblue] more implementation for this guy
2025-11-19 10:09:53 [simon@midnightblue] class NitroPageAllocator : public v8::PageAllocator {public:	size_t AllocatePageSize() override {		return 4096;	}	size_t CommitPageSize() override {		return 4096;	}	void SetRandomMmapSeed(int64_t seed) override {		std::cout << "SetRandomMmapSeed" << std::endl << std::flush;	}	void* GetRandomMmapAddr() override {		std::cout << "GetRandomMmapAddr" << std::endl << std::flush;		return nullptr;	}	void* AllocatePages(void* address, size_t size, size_t alignment, Permission permissions) override {		std::cout << "AllocatePages" << std::endl;		int prot = PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE; // Default to RW; adjust based on permissions if needed		void* addr = mmap(address, size, prot, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);		return addr == MAP_FAILED ? nullptr : addr;	}	bool FreePages(void* address, size_t size) override {		return munmap(address, size) == 0;	}	bool DeallocatePages(void* address, size_t size) {		return FreePages(address, size);	}	bool ReleasePages(void* address, size_t size, size_t new_size) override {		// Shrink mapping if possible		if (new_size < size) {			return munmap(static_cast<char*>(address) + new_size, size - new_size) == 0;		}		return true;	}	bool DecommitPages(void* address, size_t size) override {		// Decommit by setting to PROT_NONE		return mprotect(address, size, PROT_NONE) == 0;	}	bool SetPermissions(void* address, size_t size, Permission permissions) override {		std::cout << "setpermissions" << std::endl;		int prot = 0;		if (permissions & 1) prot |= PROT_READ;		if (permissions & 2) prot |= PROT_WRITE;		if (permissions & 4) prot |= PROT_EXEC;		return mprotect(address, size, prot) == 0;	}};
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] Here are the main things to tighten up for `NitroPageAllocator` on a POSIX‐like embedded system,
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] assuming sandbox + pointer compression are enabled and you’re happy to let the kernel pick the
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] actual addresses.
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] Key goals:
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] 
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Honour `permissions`.
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Respect `alignment` (at least to page size, usually more).
2025-11-19 10:10:30 [gpt-5.1-2025] - Provide a usable `GetRandomMmapAddr` implementation (not `nullptr`).
