2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] anonymous memory, effectively wiping out any data (such as JIT code) that was previously written
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] there.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Correction: This should typically use `mprotect(address, size, prot)` to change the
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] permissions of the existing pages without overwriting the content.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  `CreateJobImpl` and `v8::JobHandle`
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     The method `CreateJobImpl` wraps the `jobtask` in a single worker task and returns
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] `std::makeunique<v8::JobHandle>()`.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Issue: `v8::JobHandle` is an abstract base class with pure virtual methods (like
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] `NotifyConcurrencyIncrease`, `Join`, `Cancel`). You cannot instantiate it directly.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Impact: This code will likely fail to compile. You need to define a concrete class
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] inheriting from `v8::JobHandle` that manages the state of the job and allows V8 to wait for
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] completion.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  `MainThreadTaskRunner` Synchronicity
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     Your `MainThreadTaskRunner::PostTask` executes `task->Run()` immediately.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Context: While efficient for simple scripts, strictly synchronous execution can
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] cause re-entrancy issues or stack overflows if V8 expects the task to be queued and run later
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] (e.g., during microtask checkpoints).
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  macOS JIT Support
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro]     It is good to see `MAP_JIT` included in `NitroPageAllocator::AllocatePages`. This is required
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] for V8 to function on Apple Silicon.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] Let me know if you would like a code snippet for a concrete `JobHandle` implementation or the
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] `mprotect` fix.
2025-11-20 15:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-20 15:34:55 [simon@midnightblue] hi kimi, can you summarise
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] Summary of the new header:
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] - Adds a custom `NitroThreadPool` (worker threads + delayed-task priority queue)
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] - Provides two `PageAllocator` variants; `NitroPageAllocator` is the richer one (handles `MAP_JIT`,
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] alignment, partial `munmap`, etc.)
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] - Supplies a no-op `TracingController` (`NitroTrace`)
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] - Implements `v8::Platform` (`NitroPlatformWithPool`) that wires everything together and exposes a
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] synchronous main-thread `TaskRunner`
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] - Main deviations from a default platform: user-controlled thread count, explicit delayed-task
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] support, custom memory-mapping logic
2025-11-20 15:35:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:36:06 [simon@midnightblue] i think it needs custom JobHandle?
2025-11-20 15:36:13 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—`v8::JobHandle` is an abstract interface, so returning `std::make_unique<v8::JobHandle>()`
2025-11-20 15:36:13 [kimi-k2-0905] won’t compile.
2025-11-20 15:36:13 [kimi-k2-0905] You need a concrete class that inherits from it and implements the pure virtuals (`Join`, `Cancel`,
2025-11-20 15:36:13 [kimi-k2-0905] `NotifyConcurrencyIncrease`, etc.).
2025-11-20 15:36:13 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:36:40 [simon@midnightblue] can you suggest a NitroJob impl
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] // NitroJob.h
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] #pragma once
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <v8.h>
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <future>
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <atomic>
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <memory>
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] class NitroJobHandle : public v8::JobHandle {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] public:
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	explicit NitroJobHandle(std::unique_ptr<v8::JobTask> task, NitroThreadPool* pool)
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		: task_(std::move(task)), pool_(pool), joined_(false) {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		// Kick off one worker to start
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		PostTask();
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	void NotifyConcurrencyIncrease() override {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		// Simple policy: spawn one more worker per call
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		PostTask();
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	void Join() override {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lk(m_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		joined_ = true;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		// Wait until task reports completion
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		cv_.wait(lk, [this] { return !task_; });
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	void Cancel() override {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lk(m_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		cancelled_ = true;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		task_.reset();          // drop the task
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		cv_.notify_all();
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	bool IsCompleted() override {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(m_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		return !task_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	bool IsRunning() override {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(m_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		return !cancelled_ && !!task_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	uint32_t GetMaxConcurrency() const override {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		// V8 usually wants 1 for simple jobs
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		return 1;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] private:
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	void PostTask() {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		pool_->PostTask(std::make_unique<v8::Task>([this] { Worker(); }));
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	void Worker() {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		std::unique_ptr<v8::JobTask> local_task;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		{
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 			std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(m_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 			if (cancelled_ || !task_) return;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 			local_task = std::move(task_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		local_task->Run(local_task.get());   // V8 passes the task itself
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		{
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 			std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(m_);
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 			task_.reset();
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 			cv_.notify_all();
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 		}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::mutex m_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::condition_variable cv_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::unique_ptr<v8::JobTask> task_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	NitroThreadPool* pool_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::atomic<bool> cancelled_{false};
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	bool joined_;
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] };
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] Use inside `CreateJobImpl`:
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] std::unique_ptr<v8::JobHandle>
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] NitroPlatformWithPool::CreateJobImpl(v8::TaskPriority,
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905]                                     std::unique_ptr<v8::JobTask> job_task,
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905]                                     const v8::SourceLocation&) {
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 	return std::make_unique<NitroJobHandle>(std::move(job_task), pool_.get());
2025-11-20 15:37:31 [kimi-k2-0905] }
