2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] Received. I have analyzed the BOMs, netlists, and logic descriptions for Project Fifteen, LUMA2,
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] CBM Node, and Project Toast.
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] Here are observations regarding the new and specific content in these designs:
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Project LUMA2 Chroma Mod: The addition of the AC-coupled comparator (U3) with a bias
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] network is a significant architectural change. It shifts the burden of color decoding from analog
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] capture to high-speed digital timing analysis (PIO edge counting within a ~280ns window) to
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] approximate the chroma index.
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Project Toast Timing: The reliance on 4x cascaded 74HC165 shift registers to capture
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] the entire Address (A0-A15) and Data bus introduces a tight timing constraint. The RP2040 must
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] latch, shift in ~32 bits, determine the memory map logic (ROML/H, EXROM, GAME), and potentially
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] drive the 74LVC245 transceiver, all within the valid data window of the 1MHz PHI2 clock.
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Project Fifteen Logic: The defined GPIO logic (GPIO High = IEC Low) is consistent with
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] the 2N7000 N-Channel FET usage for open-drain bus driving.
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  CBM Node: The hybrid approach using shift registers for the parallel User Port
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] (PB0-PB7) and direct FETs for the handshake lines (PA2, CNT, SP) effectively isolates the 5V logic
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] while maintaining bidirectional capability via the 74LVC245.
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] The netlists match the provided BOMs and pin allocations.
2025-11-30 12:58:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:01:13 [simon@midnightblue] thanks, a bulk transfer on node on cia means the c64 could decide where to write the bytes
2025-11-30 13:01:45 [simon@midnightblue] how do i clock data on the user port
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Based on your CBM Node netlist, you have a specific setup where the RP2040 drives signals
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] via Open Drain (2N7000) and reads signals via Shift Registers (74HC165).
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] To perform a bulk transfer where the C64 accepts bytes (e.g., loading a file), you should use the
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] standard CIA Handshake Protocol utilizing `FLAG` and `PA2`.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] The Handshake Logic
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Data Bus (PB0-PB7): Carries the byte.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Clock/Strobe (RP2040 → C64): Use FLAG2 (Pin B).
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro]        Netlist:* GP15 → 2N7000 → FLAG2.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro]        Logic:* Pulse Low to tell C64 "Data is ready".
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Acknowledge (C64 → RP2040): Use PA2 (Pin M).
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro]        Netlist:* C64 PA2 → Shift Register U2 Pin 13.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro]        Logic:* C64 pulls Low (or toggles) to say "I have the data".
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Protocol Steps
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 1. RP2040 Side (Sender)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Since you read the C64's status via a Shift Register (U2), you cannot detect microsecond pulses.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] You should use a State Change (Toggle) protocol for the Acknowledge.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Write Data: Output byte to 74LVC245 (GP2-GP9) and enable output (GP16 LOW).
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Signal C64: Pulse GP15 (FLAG2) LOW for ~1µs, then release (High-Z).
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro]        Note:* This triggers the IRQ or sets the Flag bit on the C64 CIA2.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Wait for ACK: Continuously read Shift Register U2. Wait for PA2 bit to
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] change state (or go Low depending on C64 code).
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 2. C64 Side (Receiver)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 CIA2 can handle this automatically if configured, or you can bit-bang.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Method A: Automatic Handshake (Fastest)*
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Configure CIA2 Port B for "Handshake" mode. When the C64 CPU reads Port B, the CIA automatically
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] pulses PA2 Low.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] ; C64 Assembly (Receiver)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] ; CIA2 Base: $DD00
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] RX_INIT:
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda #$00       ; Set Port B (Data) to Input
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $DD03      ; DDRB
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $DD00      ; Set PA2 (Pin M) to Output logic
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	ora #$04       ; Ensure PA2 is output (DDR A bit 2)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $DD00
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	; Configure CIA Control Register A (CRA)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	; Bit 2: Port B Mode (1 = Handshake / Pulse PA2 on Read)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $DD0E
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	ora #$04
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $DD0E
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	rts
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] READ_BYTE:
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	; Wait for FLAG (Pin B) from RP2040
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	; FLAG sets Bit 4 of Interrupt Control Register ($DD0D)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] WAIT_FLAG:
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $DD0D      ; Read ICR
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	and #$10       ; Check Flag bit
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	beq WAIT_FLAG  ; Wait until Flag is set
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	; Reading Port B automatically pulses PA2 Low
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $DD01      ; Read Data
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	rts
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Method B: Manual Handshake (More control)*
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Use PC2 (Pin 8) or PA2 manually if the automatic pulse is too short for your RP2040 Shift Register
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] to catch.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] RP2040 Implementation (JavaScript/PIO Concept)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Since reading the ACK requires shifting in data (slow), ensure the C64 holds the line long enough.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] // RP2040 Pseudo-code for sending 1 byte
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] async function sendByteToC64(byteVal) {
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	// 1. Setup Data
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	setTransceiverData(byteVal); // Set GP2-GP9
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	gpioWrite(GP16, 0);          // Enable 74LVC245 Output (/OE)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	// 2. Capture current state of PA2 (from last shift register read)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	let lastPA2 = getShiftRegBit(PA2_INDEX);
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	// 3. Strobe FLAG2 (GP15)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	// GP15 is Open Drain: High = 1 (Off), Low = 0 (Active)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	gpioWrite(GP15, 1); // Drive Low (Active)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	sleep_us(2);
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	gpioWrite(GP15, 0); // Release (Pull-up on C64 handles high)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	// 4. Wait for Acknowledge (PA2 state change)
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	// We must continuously clock the 74HC165 to read input
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	let timeout = 1000;
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	while (timeout > 0) {
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 		shiftInRegisters(); // Pulse GP17/GP18, read GP19/GP20
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 		let currentPA2 = getShiftRegBit(PA2_INDEX);
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 		if (currentPA2 !== lastPA2) {
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 			// C64 acknowledged
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 			break;
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 		}
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 		timeout--;
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	}
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 	gpioWrite(GP16, 1); // Disable Output
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Critical Hardware Note
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] Your netlist has `GP10, PA2 out`.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] • When Sending to C64: Ensure GP10 is set to 0 (Low Logic / FET Off) so the RP2040
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] does not pull PA2 low. Let the C64 drive PA2 so the RP2040 can read it via U2.13.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] • When Receiving from C64: The RP2040 can drive GP10 to High (FET On) to signal the C64, or
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] use PC2/FLAG logic reversed.
2025-11-30 13:02:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:05:30 [simon@midnightblue] i would like to add setup steps to the guide for software dev angle on the device
2025-11-30 13:06:42 [simon@midnightblue] sequence of csv for the bulk read and bulk write methods
2025-11-30 13:06:49 [simon@midnightblue] steps
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Based on the CBM Node netlist and BOM, here is the guide for clocking data and the software
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] development sequences.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Clocking Concept: The Interlocked Handshake
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Because the RP2040 reads the C64 control signals (`PC2`, `SP1`, `SP2`) via a 74HC165 Shift
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Register (rather than direct GPIO interrupts), the RP2040 cannot react instantly to a clock
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] edge.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Therefore, you cannot use a synchronous clock (like SPI) effectively. You must use a Fully
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Interlocked Handshake.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  FLAG2 (RP2040 Output -> C64 Input): Connected to GP15. Pulsing this low triggers an
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] interrupt (or sets a bit) on the C64 CIA2. Used to tell C64 "Data is ready" or "I am ready".
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  PC2 (C64 Output -> RP2040 Input): Connected to Shift Register U2.5. The C64 CIA pulses
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] this low automatically when writing to Port B.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  PA2 (Bidirectional): Connected to Shift Register U2.13 (Input) and GP10 (Output). Used
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] as a generic Acknowledgement line.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Developer Guide: Setup
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] • 1. GPIO Initialization*
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] • Bus Transceiver (74LVC245): Set `/OE` (GP16) HIGH (Disable) initially. Set `DIR`
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] (Hardwired 3V3) implies A->B (RP2040 to C64). Note: The BOM says 74LVC245 DIR is 3V3, meaning
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] it effectively drives C64. To Read C64, you must toggle /OE. Wait, the 74LVC245 is strictly Output
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] from RP2040 to C64 based on your netlist. The Inputs come via the 74HC165s.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] • Shift Registers (74HC165): Initialize SPI/PIO to read these constantly.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] • Control Lines: Set `FLAG2` (GP15) and `PA2` (GP10) LOW (Logic High on bus due to FET
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] inversion) to start.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Sequence CSV: Bulk Write (C64 sending to RP2040)
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] In this mode, the C64 controls the flow. The RP2040 acts as a passive listener until data is
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] latched.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] • Assumption:* `PA2` is used by RP2040 to Acknowledge receipt.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Actor,Action,Signal State,Description
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 1,C64,Set Data,PB0-PB7 = DATA,C64 places byte on User Port B
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 2,C64,Assert Ready,PC2 = LOW,CIA2 pulls PC2 low (Auto or Manual) indicating data valid
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 3,RP2040,Poll Inputs,Shift Reg Read,RP2040 detects PC2 is LOW via U2.5
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 4,RP2040,Read Data,Shift Reg Read,RP2040 extracts PB0-PB7 bits from U1/U3
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 5,RP2040,Assert Ack,PA2 (GP10) = HIGH,RP2040 drives FET Q9 -> PA2 Line goes LOW (Active)
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 6,C64,Wait for Ack,Read PA2,C64 waits until PA2 goes LOW
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 7,C64,Release Ready,PC2 = HIGH,C64 finishes write cycle
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 8,RP2040,Detect Release,Shift Reg Read,RP2040 sees PC2 return HIGH
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 9,RP2040,Release Ack,PA2 (GP10) = LOW,RP2040 turns off FET -> PA2 Line goes HIGH (Passive)
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
