2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] C64 Implementation Notes (BASIC/Asm)
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Bulk Write (C64 -> RP2040):
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Set CIA2 Port B DDR (DD03) to FF (All Output).
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Store Byte in Port B ($DD01).
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The CIA automatically pulses `PC2` low for one cycle on write, but for the "Interlocked"
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] method required by the shift registers, you might need to manually toggle `PA2` or `PC2` (if manual
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] mode enabled) to hold the line low long enough for the RP2040 to shift it in.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Bulk Read (RP2040 -> C64):
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Set CIA2 Port B DDR (DD03) to 00 (All Input).
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Enable FLAG interrupt or poll the ICR register ($DD0D).
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   When FLAG occurs, read Port B ($DD01).
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Toggle `PA2` ($DD00 bit 2) to acknowledge.
2025-11-30 13:07:34 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:10:38 [simon@midnightblue] could bulk read writing bytes at a time to ,x index by 6510 with poll be ok?
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, using `STA ,X` with polling is an excellent approach for bulk transfers on the C64. It avoids
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] the overhead of interrupt context switching (saving registers to stack), allowing for much higher
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] throughput.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] Since the RP2040 is significantly faster than the C64, the C64 dictates the speed. The RP2040 must
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] wait for the C64 to "acknowledge" receipt of a byte before sending the next.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the setup guide and the handshake logic based on your CBM Node netlist.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] Clocking Data on the User Port (CIA2)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] You have two key control lines in your netlist for flow control:
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  `FLAG2` (RP2040 Output, C64 Input): Connected to the CIA2 `FLAG` pin. A transition
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] (high-to-low) sets a bit in the CIA Interrupt Control Register (ICR).
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  `PC2` (C64 Output, RP2040 Input): Connected to the CIA2 `PC` pin. The CIA can
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] automatically pulse this low when the CPU reads/writes Port B.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • The Handshake Logic:*
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  RP2040 places data on the bus and asserts `FLAG2` (Low).
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  C64 polls the `FLAG` bit. When set, it reads the data.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  C64 (via CIA hardware) automatically pulses `PC2` low upon reading the data.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  RP2040 detects `PC2` low, de-asserts `FLAG2`, and prepares the next byte.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] Software Development Guide
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Setup Steps
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • C64 Side (CIA2 Setup):*
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • DDRB (DD03): Set to `00` (Input) for reading, `$FF` (Output) for writing.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • ICR ($DD0D): Read once to clear any pending flags.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • CRA ($DD0E): Set bit 3 (`0x08`) to enable "Handshake Mode". This forces `PC2` to pulse
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] low automatically for 1 cycle after a Read/Write of Port B.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Side:*
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • GPIO: Configure `PB0-7` (via 74LVC245/74HC165) as needed.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • IRQ: You may want an IRQ on the `PC2` input pin (Shift Register bit) to detect the C64's
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ACK immediately, or simply poll the shift register in a tight loop on one core.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Sequence: Bulk Read (RP2040 → C64)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 is the "Actor" driving the speed. The RP2040 is the "Server".
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ╭────────┬──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────╮
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  Step  │  Actor   │  Action                                  │  Signal State                   │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ├────────┼──────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  :---  │  :---    │  :---                                    │  :---                           │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  1     │  RP2040  │  Writes Byte to `PB0-PB7` (via '245)     │  Data Stable                    │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  2     │  RP2040  │  Pulls `FLAG2` Low                       │  **FLAG2 Low** (Data Ready)     │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  3     │  C64     │  Polls `$DD0D` (ICR) until Bit 4 is set  │  Detecting...                   │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  4     │  C64     │  Reads Data from `$DD01`                 │  **PC2 Pulses Low** (Auto ACK)  │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  5     │  RP2040  │  Detects `PC2` Low (via '165)            │  Acknowledge Received           │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  6     │  RP2040  │  Pulls `FLAG2` High                      │  **FLAG2 High** (Reset)         │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  7     │  RP2040  │  Loads next byte, GOTO Step 1            │                                 │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ╰────────┴──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────╯
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Sequence: Bulk Write (C64 → RP2040)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ╭────────┬──────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────╮
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  Step  │  Actor   │  Action                          │  Signal State                          │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ├────────┼──────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  :---  │  :---    │  :---                            │  :---                                  │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  1     │  C64     │  Writes Byte to `$DD01`          │  **PC2 Pulses Low** (Auto Data Ready)  │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  2     │  RP2040  │  Detects `PC2` Low (via '165)    │  Data Available                        │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  3     │  RP2040  │  Reads `PB0-PB7` (via '165)      │  Data Captured                         │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  4     │  RP2040  │  Pulses `FLAG2` Low then High    │  **FLAG2 Pulse** (Ack)                 │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  5     │  C64     │  Polls `$DD0D` for `FLAG` (Ack)  │  Waiting for buffer space              │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] │  6     │  C64     │  Loads next byte, GOTO Step 1    │                                        │
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ╰────────┴──────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────╯
