2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] C64 Assembly Implementation
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] Here is an optimized polling loop for the Bulk Read (RP2040 to C64). This uses the `STA ,X`
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] indexing you requested.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ; CBM Node Bulk Read Routine
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ; Destination: buffer ($2000)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] ; Length: 256 bytes (Y register as counter)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			*= $1000
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] RX_START	lda #$00
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			sta $dd03       ; Set Port B to Input
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; Enable Handshake mode on CIA2 control register A
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; Bit 3 = 1 (Force PC output low on Port B access)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			lda $dd0e
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			ora #$08
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			sta $dd0e
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			ldx #$00        ; Initialize X index
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] RX_LOOP
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; 1. Poll for FLAG (Data Ready from RP2040)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; Bit 4 of ICR ($DD0D) reflects the FLAG pin state latch
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] WAIT_FLAG	bit $dd0d
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			beq WAIT_FLAG   ; If Bit 4 is 0, keep waiting
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; 2. Read Byte
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; Reading $DD01 automatically pulses PC2 low (ACK to RP2040)
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			lda $dd01
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; 3. Store Byte
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			sta $2000, x
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			; 4. Loop Logic
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			inx
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			bne RX_LOOP     ; Loop until X wraps to 0
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 			rts
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Note on Speed:*
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] The RP2040 must detect the `PC2` pulse (via the shift register) and put the new data on the bus
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] before the C64 gets back to the `lda $dd01` instruction in the next iteration. Given the
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] RP2040's speed (133MHz+) vs the C64 (1MHz), the RP2040 has plenty of time to update the shift
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] registers between C64 cycles.
2025-11-30 13:11:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
