2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the breakdown for the CBM Node software development, handshake logic, and 6502
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] implementation.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Memory Control
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] Yes. Since the C64 is the "Master" in terms of bus timing for the 6510 CPU, it decides exactly
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] where to store the bytes. The RP2040 simply presents a byte at the User Port `PB0-PB7` and signals
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] that it is valid. The C64 reads register `DD01` (CIA2 Port B) and performs a `STA xxxx` to your
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] chosen buffer.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Clocking the User Port (Handshaking)
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] Based on your netlist, you have the following control lines available:
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Output (Drive): `FLAG2` (GP15), `PA2` (GP10).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Input (Read): `PC2` (Shift Register U2.5).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • The Standard Handshake Protocol:*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  FLAG2 (Pin B): Used by RP2040 to tell C64 "Data is Ready" (triggers IRQ or sets ICR
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] bit).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  PC2 (Pin 8): Used by C64 to tell RP2040 "Data Accepted" (automatically pulses low when
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] C64 reads/writes Port B if Control Register is set).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Software Development Guide (Setup Steps)
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • A. Initialization (C64 Side)*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  DDR Setup: Set CIA2 Port B (`DD03`) to Input (`00`) for reading, or Output (`$FF`) for
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] writing.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  CIA Control: Set CIA2 Control Register B (`$DD0F`) to configure handshake behavior
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] (e.g., Pulse PC2 on port access).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Interrupts: Disable CIA interrupts (`7F` to `DD0D`) if using polling (recommended for
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] high speed).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • B. Initialization (RP2040 Side)*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  GPIO Dir: Set `GP2-GP9` (Bus) as Output (to send) or Input (to receive).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Transceiver: Set `GP16` (/OE) LOW to enable the 74LVC245.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Idle State: Ensure `FLAG2` (GP15) is High (Passive).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 4. Sequence of Operations (CSV Style)
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • Scenario: Bulk Read (RP2040 sends data to C64)*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] Step, Actor, Action, Signal State
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1, RP2040, Writes Data to GP2-GP9, Bus Stable
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2, RP2040, Pulses FLAG2 Low for >1µs, FLAG2 Low -> High
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 3, C64, Detects FLAG2 (Bit poll or IRQ), CIA2 ICR Bit 4 Set
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 4, C64, Reads CIA2 Port B ($DD01), Data entering CPU
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 5, C64, HW auto-pulses PC2 Low (optional), PC2 Low -> High
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 6, RP2040, Detects PC2 Pulse (via Shift Reg), Ready for next byte
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • Scenario: Bulk Write (C64 sends data to RP2040)*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] Step, Actor, Action, Signal State
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1, C64, Writes Data to CIA2 Port B ($DD01), Bus Stable
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2, C64, Manually toggles PA2 or auto PC2, Signal Low
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 3, RP2040, Detects Signal (Shift Reg), Logic Trigger
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 4, RP2040, Latches Shift Regs, Reading Data
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 5, RP2040, Pulses FLAG2, Acknowledge
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 5. C64 Assembly Implementation
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] You asked if writing bytes to `,X` indexing with a poll is okay. Yes, this is the most efficient
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] way to transfer a 256-byte page.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • The `BIT` Command:*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] The `BIT` instruction is ideal here. It samples memory bits 6 and 7 into the CPU Status Register (V
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] and N flags) without modifying the Accumulator.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • CIA Interrupt Control Register (`$DD0D`) Bit 4 corresponds to the FLAG pin.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • However, `BIT` reflects bit 7 (N) and 6 (V).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • Standard practice: Read `$DD0D` into A to clear it, then loop reading it.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] • Example: Bulk Read 256 Bytes from RP2040*
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] ; Setup
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	SEI             ; Disable IRQs
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	LDA #$00
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	STA $DD03       ; Set Port B to Input
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	STA $DD0D       ; Clear any pending CIA interrupts
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	LDX #$00        ; Init Index
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] READ_LOOP:
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 1. Wait for RP2040 to assert FLAG2
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; FLAG2 sets Bit 4 of ICR ($DD0D).
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; We must load A to check specific bits if not Bit 6/7.
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] WAIT_FLAG:
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	LDA $DD0D       ; Read Interrupt Control Register
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	AND #$10        ; Mask Bit 4 (FLAG pin detection)
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	BEQ WAIT_FLAG   ; If zero, flag not received yet
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 2. Read Data
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	LDA $DD01       ; Read Port B (Triggers PC2 if configured)
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 3. Store Data
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	STA $C000, X    ; Write to buffer at $C000 + X
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 4. Handshake / Next
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	; (PC2 pulse happens automatically on LDA $DD01 if PCR is set)
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	INX
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	BNE READ_LOOP   ; Loop until X rolls over to 0
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	CLI             ; Re-enable IRQs
2025-11-30 13:13:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	RTS
