2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the details regarding the Cbm Node (User Port) logic, specifically focusing on the
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] handshaking, 6510 assembly timing, and the software development guide.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Clarification on "Bulk Transfer"
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] Unlike the Expansion Port (Project Toast), the User Port is not a DMA bus. The C64 CPU
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] (6510) must explicitly move every byte.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Role: Puts a byte on the 74LVC245, signals "Data Ready".
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • C64 Role: Detects signal, reads byte from `$DD01` (CIA2 Port B), writes it to memory,
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] signals "Acknowledge".
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2. 6510 Assembly Performance
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] You asked about `STA` and `BIT`. The C64 is the bottleneck. The RP2040 will spend most of its time
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] waiting for the C64.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Cycle Counts (PAL C64 ~0.985 MHz):*
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • `STA $abs` : 4 cycles (~4 µs)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • `STA $abs, X` : 5 cycles (~5 µs) <-- You will use this for bulk storage
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • `BIT $abs` : 4 cycles (~4 µs)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • `LDA $abs` : 4 cycles (~4 µs)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • `BVC/BPL` : 2 cycles (no branch), 3 cycles (branch taken)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Theoretical Max Speed (Polled Loop):*
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] A tight "Unrolled" loop is faster, but a standard indexed loop looks like this:
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] ; X = 0
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] LOOP:   BIT $DD0D     ; 4 cycles - Check Interrupt Control Reg (FLAG detection)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]         BVC LOOP      ; 3 cycles - Wait for Flag (Branch if V clear)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]         LDA $DD01     ; 4 cycles - Read Byte from User Port
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]         STA $0400, X  ; 5 cycles - Store in screen memory (or buffer)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]         ; Pulse PA2 here to ACK if needed (4+ cycles)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]         INX           ; 2 cycles
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]         BNE LOOP      ; 3 cycles
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Total:* ~21 to 25 cycles per byte.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Throughput:* ~40KB/s to 50KB/s.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3. How to Clock Data (The Handshake)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] Based on your netlist, you have:
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 -> C64: `FLAG2` (Pin B, via GP15/2N7000). This sets the "Flag" bit in CIA2 ICR.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • C64 -> RP2040: `PA2` (Pin M, via GP10/2N7000) or `PC2` (Pin 8, via Shift Reg).
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommended Protocol (RP2040 sending to C64):*
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  RP2040 writes byte to 74LVC245.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  RP2040 asserts `FLAG2` (Low Pulse).
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  C64 detects `FLAG` (via `BIT $DD0D` bit 4 or IRQ).
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  C64 reads Port B (`$DD01`).
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  C64 toggles `PA2` (output) to acknowledge.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 6.  RP2040 detects `PA2` change, prepares next byte.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4. Sequence CSV (Protocol Definition)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Scenario: Bulk Read (C64 reading stream from RP2040)*
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Actor,Action,Signal State,Notes
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1,RP2040,Write Data to Bus,GP2-GP9 (Data) Set,74LVC245 driving User Port
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2,RP2040,Signal Data Ready,GP15 (FLAG2) LOW,Triggers CIA2 Flag latch
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3,C64,Poll for Flag,Reading $DD0D Bit 4,Waiting for 2N7000 pull-down
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4,RP2040,Release Flag,GP15 (FLAG2) HIGH,Pulse complete
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 5,C64,Read Data,LDA $DD01,C64 takes byte
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 6,C64,Ack Data,Toggle PA2 ($DD00 Bit 2),Tells RP2040 byte consumed
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 7,RP2040,Detect Ack,Read GP10 (PA2),RP2040 loop proceeds
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 8,C64,Store Data,STA Buffer,X,Write to memory
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Scenario: Bulk Write (C64 sending stream to RP2040)*
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Actor,Action,Signal State,Notes
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1,C64,Write Data,STA $DD01,Data on User Port traces
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2,C64,Signal Ready,Toggle PA2 ($DD00 Bit 2),Handshake line
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3,RP2040,Detect Ready,Read GP10 (PA2),Polls or IRQ on PA2 change
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4,RP2040,Latch Data,Pulse GP18 (Shift Load),74HC165 captures PB0-PB7
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 5,RP2040,Read Data,SPI Read,Ingest data
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 6,RP2040,Ack,Pulse GP15 (FLAG2),Tells C64 "I got it"
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 7,C64,Detect Ack,BIT $DD0D,Loop continues
