2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 5. Developer Guide: Setup Steps
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] C64 Side (Assembly)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Disable Interrupts: `SEI`. You don't want the kernel interfering with CIA2.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Configure Port B (Data): Write `00` to `DD03` (All inputs) for reading, or `$FF` for
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] writing.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Configure Port A (Control): Ensure PA2 is output. `DD02` usually defaults to `3F` (bits
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 0-5 output). Ensure bit 2 is 1.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Clear Garbage: Read `$DD0D` once to clear any pending latched flags.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  Enter Loop: Run the polling loop defined in section 2.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] RP2040 Side (C/C++)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  GPIO Init: Set GP2-9 as Bus.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Transceiver Control:
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]        Reading from C64: Set GP21 (`/OE`) HIGH (Disable 245 output), Set GP16 (`DIR`)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] appropriately (though 245 usually fixed direction, check your wiring). Correction:* Your
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] netlist shows 74LVC245 is "Write from RP2040 -> C64". You use 74HC165 for reading C64 -> RP2040.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Logic: If sending to C64, enable 74LVC245. If reading from C64, disable 74LVC245
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] and use 74HC165.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  PIO vs Core:
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Use Core 0 for USB/Serial logic.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Use Core 1 or PIO for the tight loop monitoring `PA2` and pulsing `FLAG2`.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Timing: Ensure `FLAG2` pulse width is at least 1µs so the CIA detects it reliably.
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 6. Example C64 Receiver Code
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] // hypothetical 6502 asm syntax
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] const c64_code = `
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] RX_START
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	sei             ; Disable interrupts
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda #$00
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $dd03       ; Set Port B (Data) to Input
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $dd02
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	ora #$04        ; Ensure PA2 is Output
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $dd02
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	ldx #$00        ; Init X index
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] RX_LOOP
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 1. Wait for FLAG (RP2040 says data ready)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] WAIT_FLAG
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	bit $dd0d       ; Check ICR
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	bvc WAIT_FLAG   ; Loop if Flag bit (6 or 4 depending on register view) clear
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 2. Read Data
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $dd01       ; Read Port B
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 3. Store Data
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $0400,x     ; Store to screen
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 4. Acknowledge (Pulse PA2)
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	lda $dd00
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	eor #$04        ; Toggle PA2 bit
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	sta $dd00
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	; 5. Loop management
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	inx
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	bne RX_LOOP
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] 	rts
2025-11-30 13:15:57 [gemini-3-pro] `;
