2025-11-30 13:34:56 [simon@midnightblue] is PC signal available?
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the breakdown for the CBM Node software development, addressing the protocol,
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] timing, and specific hardware constraints of your netlist.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Protocol & Addressing (The "Header" Concept)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 User Port is a raw stream. The C64 does not know "where" to put data automatically. You
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] must implement a software protocol (a header) sent before the bulk data.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Sequence:*
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Command Byte: e.g., `0x01` (Write Memory), `0x02` (Read Memory).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Address Low: `0x00`
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Address High: `0xC0` (Start at $C000)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Length Low: `0xFF`
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  Length High: `0x00` (255 bytes)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 6.  Payload: [Data Stream...]
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • C64 Side Logic:*
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] The 6510 CPU reads the first 5 bytes, sets up a Zero Page pointer (e.g., `FB/FC`), and then enters
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] the tight read loop.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Dev Guide: Setup & CSV Sequence
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Hardware Setup:*
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040: Configure GP2-GP9 as Output (Data). Configure GP17-GP20 for SPI (Shift
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Registers).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • C64: Configure CIA2 Port B (User Port) as Input (`STA DD03, #00`).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • CSV / Logic Flow (Bulk Write to C64):*
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  IDLE: RP2040 reads Shift Register (U2). Checks `PC2` (Pin 8) or `FLAG2` status to
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] ensure C64 is listening.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  PREPARE: RP2040 puts data byte on GP2-GP9.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  STROBE: RP2040 pulses `PA2` (GP10) LOW then HIGH. This triggers the CIA interrupt or
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Flag bit on C64.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  WAIT: RP2040 continuously reads Shift Register (U2) waiting for C64 handshake (usually
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] `PC2` going Low then High) before sending next byte.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Performance: `STA` and Polling
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Is `STA ,X` fast enough? Yes.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • 6502 Timing:
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `LDA $DD01` (Read Port B): 4 cycles
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `STA $C000, X` (Store absolute indexed): 5 cycles
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `INX` (Increment Index): 2 cycles
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `BNE` (Loop): 3 cycles
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Total: ~14-20 cycles per byte.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Speed: At 1MHz, 20 cycles = 50,000 bytes/second (approx 50KB/s) theoretical max.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Bottleneck: The bottleneck is not the `STA`; it is the synchronization. The RP2040 is
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 133x faster than the C64. The RP2040 will spend 99% of its time waiting for the C64 to finish the
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] `STA`.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 4. Dual Serial (SP1 & SP2)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 has two CIAs (Complex Interface Adapters).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • SP1: CIA #1 Serial Port (User Port Pin 5).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • SP2: CIA #2 Serial Port (User Port Pin 7).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Concept:*
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] These are hardware shift registers inside the C64. They work independently of the parallel Port B.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Simultaneous: Yes, they can operate at the same time.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Direction: Each SP pin can be Input or Output, but not both at once.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Full Duplex: You can set SP1 to Read (C64 listening) and SP2 to Write (C64 talking). This
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] allows bidirectional traffic without switching modes.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Double Bandwidth: Set both to Read. You can transfer 2 bits at a time (serial streams)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] alongside the 8-bit parallel port, though synchronizing all three is complex.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 5. Hardware Check: PC Signal
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Is the `PC` signal available?
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Netlist Check: `U2.5, P6, PC2 (8)`.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Result: Yes, but it is connected to the 74HC165 Shift Register, not a
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] direct GPIO.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • Implication: The RP2040 cannot use a PIO `WAIT` instruction on PC2. The RP2040 CPU must
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] repeatedly read the SPI shift register to detect the PC2 handshake.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 6. PIO Code (Write Loop)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Since `PC2` is not on a direct GPIO, the PIO cannot handle the full handshake automatically.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] However, the PIO can handle the high-speed output and strobing, while the C code governs
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] the flow control via the shift registers.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a PIO program to drive the 74LVC245 (Data) and pulse PA2 (Handshake).
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] // cbm_node.pio
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] .program cbm_write_byte
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] .side_set 1 opt
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] ; Configuration:
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] ; - OUT pins: GP2-GP9 (8 bits, Data)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] ; - SIDESET pin: GP10 (PA2 / Handshake)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] ; - FIFO: Autopull enabled
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] public entry_point:
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pull block          ; Wait for byte from ARM core
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     out pins, 8         ; Output 8 bits to GP2-GP9
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     ; Pulse PA2 Low (Signal Data Ready to C64)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     ; Assuming 2N7000 inverts logic: GPIO High = Line Low
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     ; Netlist: GP10 High -> 2N7000 On -> PA2 Low
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     set pins, 1  [4]    ; Drive GP10 HIGH (PA2 Low) for a few cycles
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     set pins, 0         ; Drive GP10 LOW (PA2 High/Float)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     ; Note: We cannot WAIT for PC2 here because it is on the SPI Shift Reg.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     ; The ARM core must not push the next byte to FIFO until
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     ; it reads the Shift Register and confirms C64 is ready.
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] • C-SDK Setup:*
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] void cbm_pio_init(PIO pio, uint sm, uint offset, uint pin_base, uint pin_pa2) {
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pio_sm_config c = cbm_write_byte_program_get_default_config(offset);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     // Map OUT pins (GP2-GP9)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     sm_config_set_out_pins(&c, pin_base, 8);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     for(int i=0; i<8; i++) pio_gpio_init(pio, pin_base+i);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pio_sm_set_consecutive_pindirs(pio, sm, pin_base, 8, true);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     // Map SET/SIDESET pin (GP10 / PA2)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     sm_config_set_set_pins(&c, pin_pa2, 1);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pio_gpio_init(pio, pin_pa2);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pio_sm_set_consecutive_pindirs(pio, sm, pin_pa2, 1, true);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     // FIFO config
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     sm_config_set_out_shift(&c, true, true, 8); // Shift right, autopull, 8 bits
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     sm_config_set_clkdiv(&c, 10.0f); // Slow down slightly for signal integrity
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset, &c);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] // Pseudo-code for Main Loop
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] void send_bulk_data(uint8_t *data, size_t len) {
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]         // 1. Wait for C64 Ready (Read Shift Register U2)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]         while( !read_pc2_from_shift_reg() ) {
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]             tight_loop_contents();
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]         }
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]         // 2. Push byte to PIO (Drives Data + Pulses PA2)
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]         pio_sm_put_blocking(pio0, sm, data[i]);
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro]     }
2025-11-30 13:35:43 [gemini-3-pro] }
