2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the information regarding the Commodore 64 User Port and specific modems.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] Common User Port Devices
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] The User Port (PB0-PB7, plus handshaking lines) exposes the CIA chip and is typically used for
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] RS-232 communications or parallel I/O. Common devices include:
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Modems: Commodore 1650, 1660, 1670, and various third-party Hayes-compatible modems
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] (often requiring a voltage level converter).
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Printer Interfaces: Centronics parallel printer adapters (e.g., Cardco, Xetec).
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Audio Devices: 8-bit sound samplers and digitizers.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Modern Hardware: Wi-Fi modems (simulating RS-232 over Telnet) and MP3 player modules.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • controllers: EPROM programmers and relay boards.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] Commodore 1650 (Automodem) Programming
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] The 1650 is a 300 baud "dumb" modem. It does not contain an internal command set (such as Hayes AT
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] commands).
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Programming Guide: There is no specific programming guide for the hardware itself.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] Control relies entirely on the C64 KERNAL RS-232 routines.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Method: You must manipulate the CIA registers directly or use KERNAL calls (`OPEN`,
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] `CHKIN`, `CHKOUT`, `BASIN`, `BSOUT`) to handle pulse dialing and data transfer. The Commodore
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 64 Programmer's Reference Guide is the essential resource for this.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] Commodore 1670 Programming
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] The 1670 is a 1200 baud "smart" modem.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Command Set: It uses a subset of the industry-standard Hayes AT command set.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Documentation: The user manual included with the 1670 contains the supported AT commands
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] (e.g., `ATDT` for tone dialing) required to program or control the modem via terminal software.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] Fastest KERNAL Baud Rate
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] The standard C64 KERNAL RS-232 routines are software-driven (bit-banging) rather than
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] hardware-driven.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Reliable Speed: 1200 baud.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Technical Limit: While the KERNAL supports settings for 2400 baud, the standard routines
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] are notoriously unstable at this speed due to video interrupts and NMI timing issues. Higher speeds
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] (9600+) require custom software drivers or hardware UART cartridges (like the SwiftLink) that
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] bypass the standard KERNAL routines.
2025-11-30 13:45:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
