2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Programmers: EPROM programmers.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Audio: Sound samplers and digitizers (e.g., The Voice Master).
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] Commodore 1650 Programming
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] The 1650 "Automodem" is a 300-baud "dumb" modem. It does not contain an internal microcontroller
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] for command processing (like AT commands).
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Programming Guide: There is no specific command guide for the device itself.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Control: It is controlled entirely by the C64 KERNAL RS-232 routines. You program it by
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] opening a logical file to device 2 and manipulating the User Port lines directly for dialing (pulse
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] only).
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Reference: The Commodore 64 Programmer's Reference Guide (Chapter 6) serves as
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] the technical manual for operating this modem.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] Commodore 1670
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] The 1670 is an intelligent 1200-baud modem.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Command Set: It supports a subset of the Hayes (AT) command set.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Documentation: It has a specific user manual detailing its dip switches and supported AT
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] commands.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] KERNAL Baud Rate Limits
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Theoretical Max: The stock C64 KERNAL RS-232 routines allow for a setting of 2400 baud.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Practical Max: 2400 baud is notoriously unstable on the stock KERNAL due to the lack of a
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] hardware UART and interference from the VIC-II video chip.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Reliable Limit: 1200 baud is generally considered the reliable limit for standard
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] KERNAL routines. Higher speeds (9600+) require custom software drivers (like those found in
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] Novaterm or ccgms) and often hardware flow control.
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:48:05 [gemini-3-pro] Emulating 1670 with CBM Node (Wi-Fi)
