2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Existing Devices for the User Port*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Modems: Commodore 1650, 1660, 1670, and modern Wi-Fi modems.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Adapters: RS-232 level converters (TTL to RS-232) and Centronics parallel printer
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] interfaces (such as the GeoCable).
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Audio/Utility: Sound samplers (digitizers), EPROM programmers, and relay control boards.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • 1650 Programming Guide*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] Yes. The 1650 Automodem manual covers basic operation. For software control, it relies on the
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] standard C64 KERNAL RS-232 routines. The technical programming details are documented in the
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] Commodore 64 Programmer's Reference Guide (Chapter 6).
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • The 1670 Modem*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] The 1670 is a 1200 baud modem. Unlike the 1650, it utilizes a subset of the Hayes "AT" command set,
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] allowing for intelligent control and auto-dialing.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Fastest Baud Rate Supported by KERNAL*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] The standard KERNAL lookup table supports up to 2400 baud. However, because the User Port
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] relies on software "bit-banging" rather than a hardware UART, 1200 baud is the practical
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] limit for reliability. Higher speeds usually require custom drivers or cartridge-based hardware
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] (like the SwiftLink).
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Emulating 1670 with CBM Node*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] Yes. Modern Wi-Fi modems (often using ESP8266/ESP32 modules) connect to the User Port and emulate
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] the Hayes AT command set. They function similarly to a 1670 but translate the serial stream to
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] Telnet/TCP.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Basic Telnet Terminals*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • CCGMS: widely considered the standard for User Port Wi-Fi modems. It is robust and simple
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] to configure.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Commercial Terminals*
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] While most are now available as freeware, these were the primary commercial-grade options:
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • Novaterm: A powerful terminal with extensive emulation options.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • DesTerm: Features a windowed, mouse-driven interface.
2025-11-30 13:50:47 [gemini-3-pro] • VIP Terminal: An early standard for C64 communications.
