2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] Shift Registers: 5 or 6?
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] You are correct, you need 6 shift registers (74HC165) to cover the full width of the bus as
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] described in your netlist:
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  U1: Address Low (A1–A8)
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  U2: Address Mid (A9–A16)
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  U3: Address High (A17–A23)
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  U4: Data Low (D0–D7)
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  U5: Data High (D8–D15)
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 6.  U6: Control Lines (/CE, /OE, /LWR, etc.)
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] • 5 registers would only provide 40 bits of input, which is insufficient for the ~47 bits of data
2025-12-01 22:37:08 [gemini-3-pro] you need to read.*
