2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Megadrive Cartridge Physical Specs
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Total Pins: 64 pins (Double-sided edge connector).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Layout: 32 pins on the Top (Side B), 32 pins on the Bottom (Side A).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Pitch: 2.54mm (0.1").
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Megadrive Line Breakdown
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the breakdown of the lines required for the bus interface.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Address Bus: 23 Lines (A1 through A23).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]        Note:* A0 does not exist physically; it is encoded via the `/LWR` and `/UWR`
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] signals.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Data Bus: 16 Lines (D0 through D15).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Control & Power Lines:
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/CE` (Cartridge Enable / ROM Select)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/OE` (Output Enable / Read)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/LWR` (Lower Byte Write)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/UWR` (Upper Byte Write)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/AS` (Address Strobe)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/DTACK` (Data Acknowledge - Crucial for RP2040 timing)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/VRES` (Reset from console)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/MRES` (Reset output to console)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/TIME` (Peripheral access A130xx)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `/CART` (Cartridge Detect)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `CLK` (System Clock)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `VCC` (+5V)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   `GND`
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Shift Register Math (Project Crumpet)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] You mentioned 5, then corrected to 6. 6 is correct.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] You need to capture roughly 47-48 signals:
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Address (23) + Data (16) + Control (~8) = 47 inputs.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • 6 × 74HC165 = 48 inputs.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Verdict: Perfect fit.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 4. RP2040 GPIO Availability
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Chip (Raw): 30 GPIO pins (GP0–GP29).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Raspberry Pi Pico (Board): 26 usable GPIO pins.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Exposed: GP0–GP22 and GP26–GP28.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Internal (Not available): GP23 (SMPS), GP24 (VBUS Monitor), GP25 (LED), GP29 (VSYS
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] Monitor).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Note on Crumpet: Your spec uses GP0–GP22 and GP26–GP28 effectively. You have utilized
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] every single available pin on a standard Pico.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 5. PCB Design Requirements
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] Which designs Require a PCB?
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] Designs utilizing an Edge Connector (where the PCB itself inserts into a console slot)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] require a manufactured PCB with Hard Gold Plating and beveled edges for durability and reliability.
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Project Crumpet: Yes. (Megadrive Cartridge slot).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Project Toast: Yes. (C64 Expansion slot).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Project Node: Yes. (C64 User Port edge connector).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Project Waffle: Yes. (GBA Cartridge slot).
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] • Designs like Fifteen, Joy, and Luma2 use cable connectors (DIN, DB9, RCA)
2025-12-01 22:45:29 [gemini-3-pro] and can be built on perfboard/stripboard or point-to-point wiring if desired.*
