2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Which designs need a PCB?
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] Designs that utilize edge connectors (gold fingers) as part of the board structure require
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] a manufactured PCB. Designs using standard headers or sockets can technically be built
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] point-to-point (perfboard), though a PCB is recommended for signal integrity on the shift register
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] chains.
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] • Essential (Must have PCB):
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Crumpet: Requires 64-pin edge connector (Megadrive Cart).
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Toast: Requires 44-pin edge connector (C64 Expansion).
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Node: Requires 24-pin edge connector (C64 User Port).
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Waffle: Requires 32-pin edge connector (GBA Cart).
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] • Optional (Can be Point-to-Point):
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Fifteen: Explicitly designed for point-to-point wiring.
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Joy: High complexity (wiring 5 shift registers and 24 FETs by hand is difficult but
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] possible).
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Luma2: Possible on perfboard, though comparators are sensitive to noise.
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Is standard 2-layer PCB thickness suitable?
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] The standard PCB thickness is 1.6mm (0.063").
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] • Megadrive (Crumpet): Yes. 1.6mm is the standard thickness for Genesis/Megadrive
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] cartridges. Beveled edges (chamfered) are highly recommended to preserve the console's connector
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] pins.
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] • Commodore 64 (Toast / Node): Yes. 1.6mm is the standard thickness for C64
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] expansion and user port cards.
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] • GBA (Waffle): No. 1.6mm is too thick and will damage the Game Boy Advance slot.
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro]        Required Spec:* You must order 0.8mm to 1.0mm thickness for GBA
2025-12-01 22:49:33 [gemini-3-pro] cartridges.
