2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 2. RP2040 GPIO Availability
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Silicon: The RP2040 chip has 30 GPIO pins.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Raspberry Pi Pico: Exposes 26 GPIO pins (GP0–GP22 and GP26–GP28).
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro]        GP23, GP24, GP25, and GP29 are used internally on the Pico for power regulation and
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] the LED.*
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Which designs need a PCB?
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] The following designs strictly require a PCB because the PCB itself acts as the male edge
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] connector:
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Waffle: Needs a PCB to fit the GBA slot.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Node: Needs a PCB to fit the C64 User Port edge connector.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Toast: Needs a PCB to fit the C64 Expansion Port edge connector.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Crumpet: Needs a PCB to fit the Megadrive Cartridge slot.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Joy and Luma2 are highly recommended for PCB due to component density, though not
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] strictly required for mechanical fit.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Fifteen is specified as "Point-to-point wiring, no PCB required."
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 4. PCB Thickness for Cartridges
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Megadrive & C64 (Crumpet, Node, Toast):
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   1.6mm (0.063"): This is standard PCB thickness and fits these vintage edge
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] connectors perfectly.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Requirement: You must specify Chamfered (Beveled) edges (usually 30° or
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 45°) and Hard Gold (ENIG) plating for durability on the fingers.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Game Boy Advance (Waffle):
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   0.8mm to 1.0mm: Standard 1.6mm is too thick and may damage the console's pins. You
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] must order thinner PCBs for GBA.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 5. GPIO Usage in "Node" Design
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] The Node design utilizes 23 GPIO pins, leaving 3 spares (on a standard Pico).
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] ╭───────────────────────────────┬─────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
