2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] ├───────────────────────────────┼─────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  :---                         │  :---       │  :---                                            │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **UART**                     │  2          │  GP0, GP1                                        │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **74LVC245 Data (PB0-PB7)**  │  8          │  GP2, GP3, GP4, GP5, GP6, GP7, GP8, GP9          │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **Control Outputs (FETs)**   │  6          │  GP10, GP11, GP12, GP13, GP14, GP15              │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **Shift Register Control**   │  4          │  GP17 (CLK), GP18 (SH/LD), GP19 (Q7), GP20 (Q7)  │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **Transceiver Control**      │  1          │  GP16 (/OE)                                      │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **Input Dividers**           │  2          │  GP26, GP27                                      │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **Internal (Pico)**          │  3          │  GP23, GP24, GP25                                │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] │  **Spare/Unused**             │  **3**      │  **GP21, GP22, GP28**                            │
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] ╰───────────────────────────────┴─────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 6. CPU Cores on Raspberry Pi Models
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] All three models listed are Quad-Core (4 cores).
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Raspberry Pi 4: Quad-core Cortex-A72.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Raspberry Pi 5: Quad-core Cortex-A76.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] • Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W: Quad-core Cortex-A53.
2025-12-01 23:03:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:04:35 [simon@midnightblue] speed of each ?
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] Based on the project specifications provided in your prompt, here are the answers to your technical
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] questions.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] Megadrive Cartridge Details
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Pin Count:* 64 pins (32 pins per side).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Line Breakdown:*
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Address: 23 Lines (A1–A23).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Data: 16 Lines (D0–D15).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Control & Power:
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   /CE (Cart Enable), /OE (Output Enable)
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   /LWR (Lower Write), /UWR (Upper Write)
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   /AS (Address Strobe), /DTACK (Data Ack)
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   /VRES, /MRES (Resets)
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   /TIME, /CART
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   CLK (Clock)
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VCC (+5V), GND
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Shift Register Count (Project Crumpet):*
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] You are correct, 6 shift registers are required.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • 2 for Data (16 bits).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • 3 for Address (23 bits, one input grounded).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • 1 for Control lines.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] RP2040 GPIO Availability
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Silicon Total: 30 GPIO pins (GP0–GP29).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Standard Pico Board: 26 exposed GPIO pins.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   GP0–GP22 are fully exposed.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]     *   GP26–GP28 are exposed (ADC capable).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro]        GP23, GP24, GP25, and GP29 are typically used internally for SMPS control, VBUS
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] sense, LED, and VSYS monitoring.*
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] PCB Requirements
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Designs strictly requiring a PCB:*
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] These designs rely on "gold fingers" (plated edge connectors) to insert directly into the console
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] slots.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Project Crumpet: Megadrive Cartridge (64 fingers).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Project Toast: C64 Cartridge (44 fingers).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Project Waffle: GBA Cartridge (32 fingers).
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Designs where PCB is optional (but recommended):*
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Project Joy: High component count (8 ICs) makes point-to-point difficult.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  cbm node: Uses a socket (EDAC 395), so it doesn't need gold fingers, but signal
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] integrity is better with a PCB.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Project Fifteen: Explicitly noted as "Point-to-point wiring".
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] PCB Thickness Standards
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Standard 2-Layer Thickness: 1.6mm.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Megadrive (Crumpet): 1.6mm is acceptable. Original carts vary (approx 1.2mm), but 1.6mm
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] fits most slots fine, though snug. Beveled edges are highly recommended.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Commodore 64 (Toast): 1.6mm is acceptable.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Game Boy Advance (Waffle): 1.6mm is too thick. GBA cartridges are significantly
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] thinner. You must order 0.8mm thickness PCBs for GBA projects to avoid damaging the
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] console's pins.
2025-12-01 23:05:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
