2025-12-03 17:07:12 [kimi-k2-0905] 24 mm PCB-edge length ≈ 0.945″ – that is almost exactly the Commodore 64 / VIC-20 cartridge
2025-12-03 17:07:12 [kimi-k2-0905] spacing (22 contacts × 2.54 mm = 22.86 mm contact field, 24 mm total tongue).
2025-12-03 17:07:12 [kimi-k2-0905] Millions were made, still cheap and easy to buy as gold-plated 22-edge/44-finger stock.
2025-12-03 17:07:12 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 17:08:59 [simon@midnightblue] the sx could have room for cartridge port????
2025-12-03 17:09:07 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—inside the 80 × 35 × 58 mm SXX-64:6 shell you still have ~60 × 25 × 45 mm of clear volume once
2025-12-03 17:09:07 [kimi-k2-0905] the IEC-bridge Pico-LCD stack is mounted.
2025-12-03 17:09:07 [kimi-k2-0905] A 22-edge/44-finger C64-style cartridge tongue only needs 25 mm width × 4 mm thickness × 12 mm
2025-12-03 17:09:07 [kimi-k2-0905] depth, so it drops straight into the rear wall with 2 mm PCB stand-offs and keeps the scale look.
2025-12-03 17:09:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 17:10:18 [simon@midnightblue] oh wow oh wow
2025-12-03 17:10:24 [kimi-k2-0905] Exactly—slap the 22-edge tongue on the back wall, label it “PORT 1”, and you’ve got a 1:6 luggable
2025-12-03 17:10:24 [kimi-k2-0905] that actually swallows real C64 carts (or tiny custom ones). Scale-perfect, no new mechanics, just
2025-12-03 17:10:24 [kimi-k2-0905] a plated edge and two stand-offs inside the existing shell.
2025-12-03 17:10:24 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 17:14:35 [kimi-k2-0905] Only real delta is the SX→SXX-64:6 rename and the explicit “C64 Expansion Port – 44-pin edge”
2025-12-03 17:14:35 [kimi-k2-0905] bullet; everything else is already in the repo.
2025-12-03 17:14:35 [kimi-k2-0905] 
