2025-12-08 21:55:19 [simon@midnightblue] hi kimi, was vic20 expander with the machine code tools called ?
2025-12-08 21:55:22 [kimi-k2-0905] The Vic-20 RAM expansion that came with the Machine Code Monitor/Tools cartridge was the
2025-12-08 21:55:22 [kimi-k2-0905] VIC-1112 (3 KB).
2025-12-08 21:55:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:55:36 [simon@midnightblue] was there similar for c64?
2025-12-08 21:55:42 [kimi-k2-0905] Not really.
2025-12-08 21:55:42 [kimi-k2-0905] Commodore never shipped a C-64 RAM expander that also carried a machine-code monitor; the 1700/1764
2025-12-08 21:55:42 [kimi-k2-0905] REUs are pure RAM.
2025-12-08 21:55:42 [kimi-k2-0905] Third-party cartridges (e.g. “Super Snapshot”, “Final Cartridge”, “Action Replay”) added a
2025-12-08 21:55:42 [kimi-k2-0905] freezer/monitor, but they were sold separately from any RAM board.
2025-12-08 21:55:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:56:20 [simon@midnightblue] can i run the hes tools on vice 64 as a cart
2025-12-08 21:56:26 [kimi-k2-0905] HES Tools was a VIC-20-only product; the 4/8/16 K ROM images it shipped on will not even start on a
2025-12-08 21:56:26 [kimi-k2-0905] C-64.
2025-12-08 21:56:26 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want a machine-code monitor in VICE for the C-64, mount a C-64 freezer cartridge (Action
2025-12-08 21:56:26 [kimi-k2-0905] Replay, Final Cartridge, Super Snapshot, etc.) instead.
2025-12-08 21:56:26 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:57:18 [simon@midnightblue] a monitor for c64 i can run from disk
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] Micromon-64 (often called just “Micromon”) is a tiny, public-domain ML monitor that loads and runs
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] from disk.
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] Grab the PRG (e.g. “micromon64.prg”), start VICE with a C-64, attach the disk image or folder, and:
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 	LOAD"MICROMON64",8
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 	RUN
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] It drops you straight to its “*” prompt; X returns to BASIC.
2025-12-08 21:57:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:27 [simon@midnightblue] on mac have a micromon_30_by_1989_pd0lur.d64 file
2025-12-08 21:59:33 [simon@midnightblue] and running vice 64
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] VICE can mount the image straight from the command line:
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] # start VICE with the disk already in drive 8
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] x64sc ~/path/to/micromon_30_by_1989_pd0lur.d64
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] or, if VICE is already running, choose
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] File → Attach disk image → Drive 8… and pick the same file.
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] The disk will show up as `0:` in CBM DOS; load the first program with
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] LOAD"*",8,1
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] RUN
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 21:59:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
