2025-12-08 22:06:28 [simon@midnightblue] hi kimi, what are basin=c commands for micromon on c64
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Micromon’s “Basin-C” is a tiny C-like compiler that lives inside the monitor.
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] All commands are issued from the Micromon prompt (`*`) and must be upper-case.
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Basin-C management
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] BNC             enter the Basin-C sub-monitor (prompt becomes ©)
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] QUIT            leave Basin-C and return to Micromon
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] NEW             delete current source
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] LOAD "name"     load source from disk
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] SAVE "name"     write source to disk
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] LIST            show whole program
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] LIST n-m        show lines n to m
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] RUN             compile to 6510 and execute (code starts at $1000)
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] COMPILE         compile only, leave code in memory
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Editor (inside © prompt)
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] n  statement    insert/replace line n
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] n               delete line n
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] AUTO n          start auto-numbering from n
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] RENUM           renumber whole program in 10’s
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] FIND "text"     search
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Language limits
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - 16-bit ints only, no floats
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - MAX 126 source lines, 32 labels, 256 bytes of globals.
2025-12-08 22:06:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:19 [simon@midnightblue] w key seems to do somethin
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] In Micromon the w command is a one-letter shortcut for
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] W <start> <end> <filename>
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] It writes (saves) a block of memory to disk as a raw binary file.
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] Example
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] W 0800 0FFF MYDATA
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] saves 2 kB from 0800–0FFF to disk as “MYDATA”.
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] If you just type W and hit RETURN you’ll get the prompt
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] START END FILENAME:
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] so it looks like “something happened” while it’s actually waiting for the three parameters.
2025-12-08 22:08:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:12:12 [simon@midnightblue] vice c64 reset key?
2025-12-08 22:12:16 [kimi-k2-0905] In VICE the reset keys are:
2025-12-08 22:12:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:12:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - Alt-Home → soft-reset (RUN/STOP + RESTORE)
2025-12-08 22:12:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - Ctrl-Alt-Home → hard-reset (power-cycle)
2025-12-08 22:12:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:12:33 [simon@midnightblue] 0n mac laptop
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] On a MacBook keyboard:
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - fn-Command-←  (soft reset)
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - ctrl-fn-Command-←  (hard reset)
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] (← is the “Home” key when fn is held.)
2025-12-08 22:12:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:17:03 [kimi-k2-0905] Got it—thanks for sharing.
2025-12-08 22:17:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
