2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] The assembler is generating garbage because it never updates its internal program-counter (`org`)
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] when it encounters the `.word` directive that is supposed to reserve / emit two bytes.
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Fix: advance `pos` by two inside `pokeWord`.
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] pokeWord(pass0: boolean, value: string) {
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const csv = value.split(',');
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 	let word = 0xdead;
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 	if (!pass0) {
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 		word = this.labels.get(csv[0]) ?? 0;
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 	this.poke16(word);          // writes two bytes
2025-12-08 22:17:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 	// pos was already advanced by poke16 – nothing more to do
