2025-12-08 22:54:08 [simon@midnightblue] does c64 have any monitor or disassembly tools in rom?
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] No—nothing even close.
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] The KERNAL ROM only gives you:
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] - `RESET` – runs the power-up sequence.
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] - `NMI` – enters the standard monitor on the VIC-20, but on the 64 it just hangs with a
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] black screen.
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] - `BASIC cold/warm start` – `READY.` prompt and that’s it.
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] No disassembler, no memory dump, no single-step.
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want a monitor you load one (e.g. SuperMON, Final Cartridge, VICE’s built-in monitor, etc.).
2025-12-08 22:54:20 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:55:17 [simon@midnightblue] i have drive 8 and 8:1?
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] The 1541 can hold two DOS images at once:
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] - drive 8  – unit 8, DOS 1 (the normal “drive 8” you already know).
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] - drive 8:1 – unit 8, DOS 2 (a second 256-byte directory track tucked at track 18 sector 1,
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] normally unused).
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] Most software ignores DOS 2, so unless you explicitly put files there with a dual-DOS tool you’ll
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] find 8:1 empty or identical to 8.
2025-12-08 22:55:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
